# UX-SPEC.md §Board ("Drag and drop") · BOARD.md §8 · ADR 0023 — a card is dragged to move it,
# and the drop goes down the path `[` / `]` take, with a place in the column.
#
# gpui starts a drag on the first motion after a press, and holds the preview at the offset the
# pointer had from the tile at that moment; the motions after it are what the columns hear. So
# the mid-drag frame is `press`, a short `move` onto the card's own ⋯ (the preview is held by that
# corner, as a hand would pick it up), then the `move`s into Todo that open the slot the `shot`
# photographs — the faded place FLT-1 left in Backlog, the lifted tile under the pointer, Todo's
# accent hairline and the dashed `Drop to move FLT-1 to Todo`.
#
# The pointer lands on a target's centre, which is the boundary between "before" and "after" a
# tile: at a tile's centre the slot opens after it. So a drop on Todo's first card puts FLT-1
# second in Todo — a place `]` cannot reach, since `]` always appends — and the counts plus the
# cursor on `card[1]` are the proof. Then a drag inside Todo reorders it: its last card, dragged
# up onto its first, opens the slot under that first card and lands second; nothing leaves the
# column. (Upward, because a slot opening under the pointer's path pushes the tiles below it
# down, and `drag` aims at where its target was when the drag began.)
#
# Virtual-lane only: it drags and takes shots.
fixture: board
await idle 20000
key g b
await hub_tab == Board 10000
assert lists.board.rows[0].badges[0] == "2" && lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "2"
dump before

press board.column[0].card[0]
move board.column[0].card[0].menu
move board.column[1].card[0]
move board.column[1].card[0]
shot dragging
release board.column[1].card[0]
await lists.board.rows[0].badges[0] == "1" 10000
assert lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "3"
await focused == "board.column[1].card[1]" 5000
shot dropped
dump dropped

# Within Todo: FLT-4, last, dropped on FLT-3, first, lands second.
assert lists["board.cards"].rows[2].badges[0] == "FLT-4"
drag board.column[1].card[2] board.column[1].card[0]
await lists["board.cards"].rows[1].badges[0] == "FLT-4" 10000
assert focused == "board.column[1].card[1]"
assert lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "3" && lists.board.rows[0].badges[0] == "1"
dump reordered
quit
